lects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 271\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Camden Property Trust is a mid-cap real estate business with a $9.9B market cap on $13M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +36% over the past three years and -35% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The business throws off $824M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6356 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 7.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 131% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.05214301087593342},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3972716.68},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structura